# fixedbugs, defect 2051, 2026-10-13, the reproducer.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header of the program's own holding `int fabs;` was told
# `internal error: compiling the generated C failed` at exit 2: clang's
# error at the header's line 3, its notes at the generated unit's include
# line, `included multiple times`, and a note in that file was the
# compiler's.
#
# FIX: notes at the line that includes the header, naming the error's own
# file, place clang's own declaration at the header's line: told as C's own
# `fabs`, the header refused at its line 3, exit 1, with a `guess` fix
# renaming it (`cli/builtin_name.hero`).

extern "fixedbugs-2051-a-header-that-declares-a-c-library-function-as-a-variable-is-refused.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function eight() -> i32

function main()
    print(eight())
